msgid "A band of fine streaks running with the stroke, soft at their ends, for rain, speed and hatched shading. It paints in a mixing blend mode where a mixing module is installed, so over another colour it mixes as paint does, blue over yellow turning green."
msgstr "A band of fine streaks running with the stroke, soft at their ends, for rain, speed and hatched shading. It paints in a mixing blend mode where a mixing module is installed, so over another color it mixes as paint does, blue over yellow turning green."

msgid "A block of flat colour with a torn edge, turned at random each dab so the edge never repeats."
msgstr "A block of flat color with a torn edge, turned at random each dab so the edge never repeats."

msgid "A chalk whose edge a fine paper grain breaks, every stroke meeting the same grain the way chalk meets the tooth of one sheet, for drawing and hatching on a toned ground. It paints in a mixing blend mode where a mixing module is installed, so over another colour it mixes as paint does, blue over yellow turning green."
msgstr "A chalk whose edge a fine paper grain breaks, every stroke meeting the same grain the way chalk meets the tooth of one sheet, for drawing and hatching on a toned ground. It paints in a mixing blend mode where a mixing module is installed, so over another color it mixes as paint does, blue over yellow turning green."

msgid "A dense ribbon of opaque paint with a ragged torn edge, built up dab on dab, a painter's own brush. It paints in a mixing blend mode where a mixing module is installed, so over another colour it mixes as paint does, blue over yellow turning green."
msgstr "A dense ribbon of opaque paint with a ragged torn edge, built up dab on dab, a painter's own brush. It paints in a mixing blend mode where a mixing module is installed, so over another color it mixes as paint does, blue over yellow turning green."

msgid "A document-wide filter that reads its neighbours cannot be flattened."
msgstr "A document-wide filter that reads its neighbors cannot be flattened."

msgid "A dry, scratchy band along the stroke, for catching the light on bark, wood and rough fabric. It paints in Colour Dodge, so it brightens what lies under it towards white whatever the colour picked, and lays nothing visible on white."
msgstr "A dry, scratchy band along the stroke, for catching the light on bark, wood and rough fabric. It paints in Color Dodge, so it brightens what lies under it toward white whatever the color picked, and lays nothing visible on white."

msgid "A fine line in the colour picked that catches the paper's tooth at a light touch and darkens as "
msgstr "A fine line in the color picked that catches the paper's tooth at a light touch and darkens as "

msgid "A fine line in the colour picked that catches the paper's tooth at a light touch and darkens as it is gone over again, in the manner of a pencil, for drawing and hatching."
msgstr "A fine line in the color picked that catches the paper's tooth at a light touch and darkens as it is gone over again, in the manner of a pencil, for drawing and hatching."

msgid "A fir tree stamped along the stroke at varying heights, for a forest edge in one line. The tree is drawn in tones, so only its darkest needles lay the colour at full and the rest of it reads paler."
msgstr "A fir tree stamped along the stroke at varying heights, for a forest edge in one line. The tree is drawn in tones, so only its darkest needles lay the color at full and the rest of it reads paler."

msgid "A flat brush that lays a thin veil of the colour picked and drags what is under it along, wet "
msgstr "A flat brush that lays a thin veil of the color picked and drags what is under it along, wet "

msgid "A flat brush that lays a thin veil of the colour picked and drags what is under it along, wet paint into wet paint."
msgstr "A flat brush that lays a thin veil of the color picked and drags what is under it along, wet paint into wet paint."

msgid "A fresh document, at the size, depth and colour space you pick"
msgstr "A fresh document, at the size, depth and color space you pick"

msgid "A fresh document, at the size, depth and colour space you pick in the dialog."
msgstr "A fresh document, at the size, depth and color space you pick in the dialog."

msgid "A gentler Overlay, darkening or lightening the paint underneath a little by the colour on top."
msgstr "A gentler Overlay, darkening or lightening the paint underneath a little by the color on top."

msgid "A ground of one colour to lay under a painting, set under the layer list. It holds no paint."
msgstr "A ground of one color to lay under a painting, set under the layer list. It holds no paint."

msgid "A hard round that takes paint away, thinner under a light hand. It paints in the Erase mode, so the colour picked plays no part."
msgstr "A hard round that takes paint away, thinner under a light hand. It paints in the Erase mode, so the color picked plays no part."

msgid "A hard round whose size alone follows the pen's pressure, so a stroke pressed in and let go comes to a point and shows its length and its direction. The lightest touch lays a hair a fifth of its width, in the colour picked."
msgstr "A hard round whose size alone follows the pen's pressure, so a stroke pressed in and let go comes to a point and shows its length and its direction. The lightest touch lays a hair a fifth of its width, in the color picked."

msgid "A pencil whose line catches the lit grain of the paper, thinner under a light hand. The paper shows between the grains, so the line reads lighter than the colour picked and takes the tint of the ground."
msgstr "A pencil whose line catches the lit grain of the paper, thinner under a light hand. The paper shows between the grains, so the line reads lighter than the color picked and takes the tint of the ground."

msgid "A point every stroke runs towards, for drawing in perspective"
msgstr "A point every stroke runs toward, for drawing in perspective"

msgid "A round that paints through a fine paper grain, speckled at a light touch and solid at a hard press, for laying in colour with a tooth to it."
msgstr "A round that paints through a fine paper grain, speckled at a light touch and solid at a hard press, for laying in color with a tooth to it."

msgid "A sheet or a cloth set whole in one step: its colours, grain and tooth."
msgstr "A sheet or a cloth set whole in one step: its colors, grain and tooth."

msgid "A smoky blot of uneven darkness, for clouds of colour and soft shadows."
msgstr "A smoky blot of uneven darkness, for clouds of color and soft shadows."

msgid "A soft eraser that fades paint out rather than cutting it. It paints in the Erase mode, so the colour picked plays no part."
msgstr "A soft eraser that fades paint out rather than cutting it. It paints in the Erase mode, so the color picked plays no part."

msgid "A soft round at half flow, for laying in colour."
msgstr "A soft round at half flow, for laying in color."

msgid "A soft round that blends the paint of the layer it is on and nothing else, so a glaze or a shadow on another layer is not blended into it. Where the layer is bare there is nothing to blend, and it lays the colour picked."
msgstr "A soft round that blends the paint of the layer it is on and nothing else, so a glaze or a shadow on another layer is not blended into it. Where the layer is bare there is nothing to blend, and it lays the color picked."

msgid "A soft round that lays no colour of its own and blends what is there into a gradient."
msgstr "A soft round that lays no color of its own and blends what is there into a gradient."

msgid "A soft round whose size follows the pen's pressure while its colour stays whole, "
msgstr "A soft round whose size follows the pen's pressure while its color stays whole, "

