msgstr "How the pixels are resampled. Bilinear blends neighboring pixels for a smooth result, Nearest keeps hard pixel edges and adds no new colors."

msgid "How the texture takes paint. Multiply thins the whole dab, Subtract lifts paint where the grain sits, Lightness moves the colour's lightness with the texture's, Height paints only where the texture is low, Colour Burn closes the dab over dark grain, Hard Mix Softer gives a flat fill with hard edges, and Linear Height paints whichever of Height and Multiply paints more."
msgstr "How the texture takes paint. Multiply thins the whole dab, Subtract lifts paint where the grain sits, Lightness moves the color's lightness with the texture's, Height paints only where the texture is low, Color Burn closes the dab over dark grain, Hard Mix Softer gives a flat fill with hard edges, and Linear Height paints whichever of Height and Multiply paints more."

msgid "How wide a new shape's stroke is, centred on its outline."
msgstr "How wide a new shape's stroke is, centered on its outline."

msgid "Hues are the peaks of a histogram of Oklab hue in 72 steps of five degrees round the wheel, smoothed over five. Paint under Oklab chroma 0.03 is grey and adds no hue. Two peaks are two hues while the histogram between them falls below half the lower peak. A hue under one per cent of the coloured paint is not named, and at most six are. Shares are of the whole canvas, and the spread is the arc that holds every hue, the wheel less the widest gap."
msgstr "Hues are the peaks of a histogram of Oklab hue in 72 steps of five degrees round the wheel, smoothed over five. Paint under Oklab chroma 0.03 is gray and adds no hue. Two peaks are two hues while the histogram between them falls below half the lower peak. A hue under one per cent of the colored paint is not named, and at most six are. Shares are of the whole canvas, and the spread is the arc that holds every hue, the wheel less the widest gap."

