msgid_plural "This file comes from an older Sara, which blended bright colours differently. These layers may look different: %s."
msgstr[0] "This file comes from an older Sara, which blended bright colors differently. This layer may look different: %s."
msgstr[1] "This file comes from an older Sara, which blended bright colors differently. These layers may look different: %s."

msgid "This preset's own gradient. Until a stop is edited it runs from the painting colour to the "
msgstr "This preset's own gradient. Until a stop is edited it runs from the painting color to the "

msgid "This preset's own gradient. Until a stop is edited it runs from the painting colour to the background colour and follows them."
msgstr "This preset's own gradient. Until a stop is edited it runs from the painting color to the background color and follows them."

msgid "Throw the detail away so the silhouette reads: average the canvas into flat blocks, or smooth inside each mass and keep its edges, then snap the lightness to a few steps, in colour or in grey, or cut it into a notan of two or three greys. The method and its numbers are in Preferences > Canvas and colour, and the Info docker sets the steps too."
msgstr "Throw the detail away so the silhouette reads: average the canvas into flat blocks, or smooth inside each mass and keep its edges, then snap the lightness to a few steps, in color or in gray, or cut it into a notan of two or three grays. The method and its numbers are in Preferences > Canvas and color, and the Info docker sets the steps too."

msgid "Ticked alone it smudges without painting, and Colour Rate beside it lays the brush's colour too. "
msgstr "Ticked alone it smudges without painting, and Color Rate beside it lays the brush's color too. "

msgid "Tint the grain. White leaves it as drawn, and a colour keeps its hue in the darks and the lights."
msgstr "Tint the grain. White leaves it as drawn, and a color keeps its hue in the darks and the lights."

msgid "Toggle between your view and the picture centred, fitted or at 100% as set in Preferences > Canvas and colour."
msgstr "Toggle between your view and the picture centered, fitted or at 100% as set in Preferences > Canvas and color."

msgid "Turn every colour into its opposite, so black becomes white, with alpha left where it was."
msgstr "Turn every color into its opposite, so black becomes white, with alpha left where it was."

msgid "Turn on Pop-up palette in Preferences > Brushes, and this key shows your brush slots round a colour wheel."
msgstr "Turn on Pop-up palette in Preferences > Brushes, and this key shows your brush slots round a color wheel."

msgid "Turn the hue, scale the colourfulness and lift the lightness, in Oklab so a hue keeps its brightness."
msgstr "Turn the hue, scale the colorfulness and lift the lightness, in Oklab so a hue keeps its brightness."

msgid "Turn the view anticlockwise, the way a painter turns the paper."
msgstr "Turn the view counterclockwise, the way a painter turns the paper."

msgid "Turns Colour Rate on for this brush. Off, the brush paints as if the page were not there."
msgstr "Turns Color Rate on for this brush. Off, the brush paints as if the page were not there."

msgid "Turns each channel full on where the two colours together reach white and off where they do not."
msgstr "Turns each channel full on where the two colors together reach white and off where they do not."

msgid "Turns the paint under it anticlockwise while held, Alt the other way."
msgstr "Turns the paint under it counterclockwise while held, Alt the other way."

msgid "Two lines over stored value along the bottom. The bright one is how much of a colour's "
msgstr "Two lines over stored value along the bottom. The bright one is how much of a color's "

msgid "Two lines over stored value along the bottom. The bright one is how much of a colour's chroma survives: flat up to the knee, then falling, slowly at first and faster the further Desaturation is pushed, and drawn in what a red highlight of that value comes out as. At the default knee of 1.0 it stays flat over every colour the screen can show and falls only past white. The dim one is the magnitude, a ramp to white and flat after it at every knee, because white stays white. The dashed mark is the knee, and under a knee above 1.0 a thin line rises from white to the knee with how much of a colour's ratios are held rather than clipped as the screen would clip them."
msgstr "Two lines over stored value along the bottom. The bright one is how much of a color's chroma survives: flat up to the knee, then falling, slowly at first and faster the further Desaturation is pushed, and drawn in what a red highlight of that value comes out as. At the default knee of 1.0 it stays flat over every color the screen can show and falls only past white. The dim one is the magnitude, a ramp to white and flat after it at every knee, because white stays white. The dashed mark is the knee, and under a knee above 1.0 a thin line rises from white to the knee with how much of a color's ratios are held rather than clipped as the screen would clip them."

msgid "Under a Gradient source it is where on the gradient each dab's colour is picked instead."
msgstr "Under a Gradient source it is where on the gradient each dab's color is picked instead."

msgid "Update Colourise Layer"
msgstr "Update Colorize Layer"

msgid "Use the colour space the rows above add up to."
msgstr "Use the color space the rows above add up to."

msgid "Value, in per cent from black at 0 to the colour at its brightest at 100"
msgstr "Value, in per cent from black at 0 to the color at its brightest at 100"

msgid "Values above 1.0 clip to white channel by channel, which shifts their hue: a hot orange arrives pale yellow. The roll-off holds the ratios and lets the colour go white instead. White stays white, and nothing here changes a single stored pixel. The Tonemap filter runs this same operator, as its Paper method, so a Tonemap over the whole picture does it too and the view steps aside."
msgstr "Values above 1.0 clip to white channel by channel, which shifts their hue: a hot orange arrives pale yellow. The roll-off holds the ratios and lets the color go white instead. White stays white, and nothing here changes a single stored pixel. The Tonemap filter runs this same operator, as its Paper method, so a Tonemap over the whole picture does it too and the view steps aside."

msgid "What Reset Zoom (Ctrl+0) shows, centred, and how a new or opened picture opens. "
msgstr "What Reset Zoom (Ctrl+0) shows, centered, and how a new or opened picture opens. "

msgid "What Reset Zoom (Ctrl+0) shows, centred, and how a new or opened picture opens. Ctrl+1 always shows actual pixels."
msgstr "What Reset Zoom (Ctrl+0) shows, centered, and how a new or opened picture opens. Ctrl+1 always shows actual pixels."

msgid "What a handle drag means. Normal scales, Shift keeping the proportions and Ctrl and an edge handle shearing. Shear leans an edge over from any handle. Perspective moves a corner and its neighbour the mirror way along the edge you drag it along, Shift and a corner moving the one corner. Freehand bends the picture by the nine points of its grid, which are what you drag, and Mirrored moves the opposite corner or side the other way with the one you drag. Cage bends what lies inside a cage you click round it."
msgstr "What a handle drag means. Normal scales, Shift keeping the proportions and Ctrl and an edge handle shearing. Shear leans an edge over from any handle. Perspective moves a corner and its neighbor the mirror way along the edge you drag it along, Shift and a corner moving the one corner. Freehand bends the picture by the nine points of its grid, which are what you drag, and Mirrored moves the opposite corner or side the other way with the one you drag. Cage bends what lies inside a cage you click round it."

msgid "What happens to a colour the screen or an 8 or 16-bit file cannot hold, a negative channel above all. "
msgstr "What happens to a color the screen or an 8 or 16-bit file cannot hold, a negative channel above all. "

msgid "What happens to a colour the screen or an 8 or 16-bit file cannot hold, a negative channel above all. Clip cuts each channel on its own, which is what other programs write and can turn the hue. Oklab keeps the lightness and the hue and gives up chroma until the colour fits, and is the default. View > Gamut Mapping switches between the two. Stored pixels, EXR and 32-bit TIFF are never touched."
msgstr "What happens to a color the screen or an 8 or 16-bit file cannot hold, a negative channel above all. Clip cuts each channel on its own, which is what other programs write and can turn the hue. Oklab keeps the lightness and the hue and gives up chroma until the color fits, and is the default. View > Gamut Mapping switches between the two. Stored pixels, EXR and 32-bit TIFF are never touched."

msgid "What the brush does while you hold it down. Push drags the paint along, Reconstruct restores it, Smooth straightens wobbly lines as a stabiliser would, Twirl turns it the way Direction says (the other way with Alt), Shrink pulls it towards the centre and Grow pushes it out (Alt swaps the two)."
msgstr "What the brush does while you hold it down. Push drags the paint along, Reconstruct restores it, Smooth straightens wobbly lines as a stabilizer would, Twirl turns it the way Direction says (the other way with Alt), Shrink pulls it toward the center and Grow pushes it out (Alt swaps the two)."

msgid "What the picture does to the colour. Mask lays the brush colour through its shape, Lightness Map "
msgstr "What the picture does to the color. Mask lays the brush color through its shape, Lightness Map "

msgid "What the picture does to the colour. Mask lays the brush colour through its shape, Lightness Map moves that colour by the picture's lightness, and Gradient Map paints each part in the colour the Gradient row on the Colour Dynamics page holds at that lightness. A grey picture has mid grey lightness throughout, so it maps to the gradient's middle."
msgstr "What the picture does to the color. Mask lays the brush color through its shape, Lightness Map moves that color by the picture's lightness, and Gradient Map paints each part in the color the Gradient row on the Color Dynamics page holds at that lightness. A gray picture has mid gray lightness throughout, so it maps to the gradient's middle."

msgid "What the ramp does past the release point: hold the far colour, run back to the near one, "
msgstr "What the ramp does past the release point: hold the far color, run back to the near one, "

msgid "What the ramp does past the release point: hold the far colour, run back to the near one, start again, or come out in bands rather than a blend."
msgstr "What the ramp does past the release point: hold the far color, run back to the near one, start again, or come out in bands rather than a blend."

